    "text": "(Verse 1)  \nIn the shadow of the city's glow,  \nWhere the jazz echoes through the room,  \nThe rhythm swings and the tempo flows,  \nA tale of love and a tale of loss,  \nWith a rate that's never quite the same,  \nAnd a rte that's never quite the same.  \n\n(Chorus)  \nOh, the night is a dance, the stars are bright,  \nA melody that's never quite the same.  \nWith a rate that's never quite the same,  \nAnd a rte that's never quite the same.  \n\n(Verse 2)  \nThe saxophone plays its sweet, old tune,  \nA story told in the soft, slow tune.  \nThe heart beats in time with the tune,  \nA love that's never quite the same.  \nWith a rate that's never quite the same,  \nAnd a rte that's never quite the same.  \n\n(Outro)  \nSo sing it loud, let the world know,  \nThat love and fate are never quite the same.  \nWith a rate that's never quite the same,  \nAnd a rte that's never quite the same.",
